## VERDICT: PASS

(iteration 2; iteration 1 is the Phase 240 independent reviewer's post-merge re-VETO, adopted verbatim as this phase's mandate)

---

### Executive Summary

The Phase 240 promotion merged on a replacement reviewer's narrower PASS while the original reviewer's seven-finding VETO and post-seal re-confirmation were still in flight - a messaging race recorded here as a process failure. Re-verification against main confirmed five findings live (V-1/V-2/V-4/V-5/V-6; V-3 had been fixed pre-merge in the Phase 240 amendment). This phase closes all five.

### Iteration 1 (the Phase 240 reviewer's re-VETO, adopted as mandate)

- V-1 (decisive, security-l3 class): doctrine-negative-constraints keyed NR-001/NR-002 bindingness on the retired min_model_capability field - an unsatisfiable predicate; the fabrication protections were structurally unbound. Line 20 falsely claimed skills still pin the field.
- V-2: dist_compile injected a preamble claiming a declaration that no longer exists, framed as binding only below-tier, compiled into all six host variants.
- V-4: the retired-field guard used an AND conjunction; single-field reintroduction passed silently.
- V-5: two fixture tests asserted substrings against files they authored themselves - structurally unable to fail.
- V-6: all three execution-context audit tests stubbed inspect_skill; the real seam was untested.
- V-7 (process): the bounded tribunal's sealed report (entry #642) asserted facts its checks could not observe ("tests exercise runtime behavior"; "the live corpus obeys the new governance").

### Iteration 2 closure (each demonstrated by executing the reviewer's own cited checks)

- V-1: the old predicate sentence greps to zero; the new Applicability binds NR-001/NR-002 unconditionally for the fabrication-risk set independent of model identity/host/tier/provider, citing the Phase 240 delta's binding-independence requirement; the false pin claim greps to zero (the field name survives once, as retirement history).
- V-2: "Below-Design-Tier Execution" greps to zero across qor/dist; the "Binding on Every Execution" block is compiled into every fabrication-risk variant on every host; residual min_model_capability mentions in dist are the accurate retired-field-detection prose from qor-plan Step 0.3, not live claims.
- V-3: the vendor ladder greps to zero in qor-plan (fixed pre-merge; the reviewer's re-check predated commit 03f11b54).
- V-4: dedicated single-field regression tests (each retired field alone) drive the shared detector.
- V-5: both fixtures now call the shared detection helpers; red-proof executed - neutering the detector key set turns both the violator fixture and the single-field tests red; restored green.
- V-6: two unstubbed tests drive execution_context.inspect_skill end to end against the live qor-audit contract with a controlled ExecutionContext, plus the unstubbed no-contract failure path.
- V-7: this report and the ledger amendment record entry #642's over-claims and the reviewer race; the sealed entries are not rewritten.

### Reviewer non-response disclosure

The originating reviewer was offered the branch for re-verification and pinged three times over ~30 minutes with no response. Per the announced fallback, closure was demonstrated mechanically against the reviewer's own cited checks (greps and executed tests recorded above) rather than substituting another reviewer's judgment. The verdict below rests on that executed evidence.

### Process Pattern Advisory

<!-- qor:veto-pattern-advisory -->
New pattern for the shadow genome: parallel-reviewer racing - when a dispatched reviewer stalls and a replacement is spawned, the first reviewer's later verdict can arrive after action was taken on the second's. Countermeasure adopted: never merge while any dispatched reviewer's verdict is outstanding; supersede explicitly or wait.

